{
  "artifacts": [
    {
      "path": "data/era5_jan1980_daily.nc",
      "type": "NetCDF",
      "description": "Daily-aggregated NetCDF file containing total precipitation (tp) as daily sums and 2 m temperature (t2m) as daily means for January 1980."
    }
  ],
  "user_friendly_explanation": "The script starts by checking if the input ‘data/era5_jan1980_hourly.nc’ file is actually a ZIP archive. In your run it detected the ZIP signature, unzipped it to a temporary folder, and discovered two NetCDF files inside: one holding accumulated precipitation (‘tp’) and another holding instantaneous 2 m temperature (‘t2m’). It then opened each file, resampled the hourly precipitation into daily totals and the hourly temperature into daily averages, and combined those two results into a single xarray Dataset. Finally, it wrote out the new daily-aggregated dataset to ‘data/era5_jan1980_daily.nc’ and cleaned up the temporary files. The log confirms every step completed successfully with no errors."
}

